<em>MacRumors</em> contributor Aaron Perris has uncovered an image file from Apple for an unreleased Apple TV 4K, suggesting that a new model will finally be released soon. The image is specifically for an "Apple TV 4K (4th generation)" model.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><em><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-TV-Sans-Remote-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067341" />Apple TV 4K (4th generation) image (on a gradient)</em></div><br/>
The image reveals that the Apple TV will have the same external design as the current model, with all of its upgrades expected to be internal. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/19/new-apple-tv-five-rumored-upgrades/">Rumored features</a> include an A17 Pro chip or newer, an increased 8GB of RAM, Apple Intelligence and Siri AI support, an Apple-designed N1 chip with Wi-Fi 7 support, and a revised Siri Remote. <br/>
<br/>
The current Apple TV is nearly four years old, having been announced in October 2022. It is equipped with an A15 Bionic chip and 4GB of RAM.<br/>
<br/>
With an A17 Pro chip or newer, the next Apple TV will have faster performance and hardware-accelerated ray tracing for improved graphics rendering in games.<br/>
<br/>
With the N1 chip, the Apple TV will support Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6.<br/>
<br/>
Wi-Fi 7 has increased bandwidth, in part because it allows for data transmission over the 2.4GHz, 5GHz, and 6GHz bands simultaneously with a supported device and router. Wi-Fi 7 is theoretically up to 4× faster than the current Apple TV's Wi-Fi 6, but real-world speeds are bottlenecked by internet service providers and other factors. <br/>
 <br/>
Siri AI will likely be the headline new feature on the next Apple TV, with tvOS 27 expected to gain a Siri app on the device. Siri AI is a much more intelligent and personalized version of Siri that can answer pretty much any question. The bump to 8GB of RAM will enable support for not only Siri AI, but some other Apple Intelligence features.<br/>
<br/>
A revised Siri Remote of some kind is expected alongside the new Apple TV, but it is unclear exactly what outward changes it will have, if any.<br/>
<br/>
In June, Apple raised prices on 14 products, including the Apple TV 4K. In the U.S., the Wi-Fi model with 64GB of storage now starts at &#36;199 (up from &#36;129), while the Wi-Fi + Ethernet model with 128GB of storage now starts at &#36;249 (up from &#36;149). It is unclear if the next Apple TV will maintain those prices or be even more expensive.<br/>
<br/>
